<title>FRANCE: Framatome/Cogema prolong nuclear fuel deal.</title>
<headline>Framatome/Cogema prolong nuclear fuel deal.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>French state-controlled nuclear engineering company Framatome and state-owned nuclear materials group Cogema said in a statement that they had prolonged their agreement for the joint supply of nuclear fuel until 2011.</p>
<p>The agreement concerns their GIE Fragema joint-venture for the sale of nuclear power rods for light water reactors as well as for MOX fuel.</p>
<p>On Wednesday, a French parliamentary commission had made the extension of the deal to 2011 one of nine conditions for approving a planned merger between Framatome and GEC-Alsthom, a joint venture of Alcatel Alsthom and GEC Plc.</p>
</text>
